Wire the HarmonyOS LocationKit provider into the device service.

The provider itself is new code and lives in the overlay, at
overlay/services/device/geolocation/ohos/, so it needs no patch. What follows
is only the part that has to change in files upstream already tracks:

  * services/device/geolocation/BUILD.gn builds the provider and links
    LocationKit (liblocation_ndk.so). It is a standalone is_ohos block rather
    than a branch of the WifiDataProvider chain below it, because OHOS still
    needs that chain's empty fallback to define WifiDataProviderHandle's
    static factory.

  * LocationProviderManager defaults OHOS to kPlatformOnly. The network
    provider it would otherwise select needs a Google API key that this build
    does not carry, so falling back to it would fail silently.

  * NewSystemLocationProvider() gains an OHOS arm. This is the line that
    actually reaches device::NewSystemLocationProvider(), defined in
    overlay/services/device/geolocation/ohos/location_provider_ohos.cc.

  * services/device/BUILD.gn compiles the conversion unit test.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51. Verified to apply cleanly to a
pristine tree at that tag; chromium-154-harmonyos.patch touches none of these
three files, so it should apply to an already-patched tree too.

Apply with:
  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-geolocation.patch

diff --git a/services/device/BUILD.gn b/services/device/BUILD.gn
--- a/services/device/BUILD.gn
+++ b/services/device/BUILD.gn
@@ -258,6 +258,12 @@
       "//services/device/fingerprint",
       "//third_party/protobuf:protobuf_lite",
     ]
+  }
+
+  if (is_ohos) {
+    # Only the LocationKit-to-geoposition translation is covered: it is the
+    # part with no device dependency, so it is the part a host run can check.
+    sources += [ "geolocation/ohos/geoposition_ohos_unittest.cc" ]
   }
 
   if (is_android) {
diff --git a/services/device/geolocation/BUILD.gn b/services/device/geolocation/BUILD.gn
--- a/services/device/geolocation/BUILD.gn
+++ b/services/device/geolocation/BUILD.gn
@@ -100,6 +100,20 @@
     deps += [ "//services/device/public/cpp:device_features" ]
   }
 
+  if (is_ohos) {
+    sources += [
+      "ohos/geoposition_ohos.cc",
+      "ohos/geoposition_ohos.h",
+      "ohos/location_provider_ohos.cc",
+      "ohos/location_provider_ohos.h",
+    ]
+
+    # LocationKit supplies the platform location provider only. The Wi-Fi data
+    # provider still comes from the empty fallback below, because OHOS exposes
+    # no scan API that WifiDataProviderCommon could drive.
+    libs = [ "location_ndk" ]
+  }
+
   # Platform-specific WifiDataProvider implementations.
   if (is_chromeos) {
     sources += [
diff --git a/services/device/geolocation/location_provider_manager.cc b/services/device/geolocation/location_provider_manager.cc
--- a/services/device/geolocation/location_provider_manager.cc
+++ b/services/device/geolocation/location_provider_manager.cc
@@ -89,8 +89,10 @@
       internals_updated_closure_(std::move(internals_updated_closure)),
       network_request_callback_(std::move(network_request_callback)),
       network_response_callback_(std::move(network_response_callback)) {
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_IOS)
-  // On Android and iOS, default to using the platform location provider.
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_IOS) || BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+  // On Android, iOS and HarmonyOS, default to using the platform location
+  // provider. On HarmonyOS the network provider is not an alternative: it
+  // needs a Google API key this build does not carry.
   provider_manager_mode_ = kPlatformOnly;
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
   // On Ash / Lacros, default to using the network location provider.
@@ -391,7 +393,7 @@
   CHECK(geolocation_system_permission_manager_);
   return device::NewSystemLocationProvider(
       geolocation_system_permission_manager_->GetSystemGeolocationSource());
-#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || \
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS) || \
     (BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) && BUILDFLAG(USE_DBUS))
   return device::NewSystemLocationProvider();
 #else
